## 8. Replace the demo deliberately

| Boundary | Production action |
|---|---|
| **Transport** | Implement `OrderApi` with the approved authenticated client, endpoint, schema, timeout, and circuit-breaker integration. No private API is invented here. |
| **Response mapping** | Validate actual order/account/request association and known rejection semantics. A nonblank ID is just the demo response rule. |
| **Retry / idempotency** | Confirm backend replay semantics and status reconciliation. Neither Redux request IDs nor disabled buttons provide durable server duplicate protection. |
| **Account changes** | Dispatch `ownerClosed()` before invalidating the account's feature, detach old UI, and coordinate unresolved writes before establishing another owner. Do not reset unknown outcomes as a login shortcut. |
| **App restart / navigation** | Implement approved durable recovery for unresolved operations. In-memory stores and local guards do not cover restarts, fresh stores, or another device. |
