## Security & Credential Storage

**Responsibility:** Protect credentials through approved native storage, controlled access, explicit error behavior, and a managed key lifecycle.

| Concern | Android | iOS | React Native |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Credential storage | Approved storage adapter with Android Keystore integration | Scoped Keychain items with reviewed accessibility/access controls | Approved native-backed auth adapter |
| Cryptographic keys | Keystore; hardware backing depends on device/key configuration | Keychain and supported Secure Enclave key operations | Delegates to native platform; JSI is not key protection |
| Biometric access | Policy-backed authentication with supported authenticators | LocalAuthentication / Keychain access controls as appropriate | Native adapter exposes the chosen policy |
| Cached personal data | Reviewed database/file protection and key lifecycle | Data protection, storage policy, and scoped cleanup | Approved cache encryption and key management |
| Network security | Approved TLS client and centrally maintained policy | Approved TLS client and platform trust evaluation | Native networking adapter follows the same policy |

Keystore manages keys; it is not an arbitrary token database. Keychain can store small credential values, while Secure Enclave supports particular key operations—it does not mean every generic-password item is an enclave-held key. A native interface or JSI call does not itself supply hardware-backed encryption. See [Apple's Keychain storage guidance](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/cryptokit/storing-cryptokit-keys-in-the-keychain).

### Credential contract

Use equivalent behavior across platforms: return “absent” only when an item is absent; propagate storage, access-control, corruption, and authentication failures distinctly. Writes must not erase the previous credential before a replacement is safely stored. Deletion is restricted to the application's account namespace.

**Android — `core/security/SecureCredentialStore.kt`**

```kotlin
