## Branding & Controlled Identity

**Responsibility:** Resolve an approved brand and publish a coherent set of design tokens, in-app assets, and supported platform identity choices.

Treat brand ID as configuration. Do not accept arbitrary remote colors, file paths, asset URLs, executable content, or icon names as a replacement for an approved registry.

| Surface | What can change | Constraint |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| In-app colors, logos, typography | A complete validated brand asset/token set | Maintain supported light/dark variants, accessibility, fallback, and version compatibility. |
| Android launcher icon | Supported predeclared activity aliases | Manifest configuration and launcher behavior matter; test device/launcher differences. |
| iOS launcher icon | Supported alternate icons bundled/configured in the app | Check support, use approved icon names, and handle asynchronous failure. |
| Launch screen / native splash | Build-time or platform-supported configuration | Do not promise arbitrary remotely replaced startup assets. |
| App name, package/bundle identity, store listing | Build/distribution configuration | A runtime theme switch does not change application identity. |

### Approved registry boundary

`src/core/branding/brandRegistry.ts`

```typescript
import type { ApprovedBrandId } from '../foundations/foundationSlice';

export interface BrandDescriptor {
  readonly id: ApprovedBrandId;
  readonly tokenSet: string;
  readonly logoAsset: string;
  readonly alternateIcon: string | null;
}

// Identifiers resolve through generated, bundled registries—not arbitrary file paths.
export const brands: Readonly<Record<ApprovedBrandId, BrandDescriptor>> = Object.freeze({
  core: Object.freeze({
    id: 'core', tokenSet: 'core-v1', logoAsset: 'brand.core.logo', alternateIcon: null,
  }),
  partner: Object.freeze({
    id: 'partner', tokenSet: 'partner-v1', logoAsset: 'brand.partner.logo', alternateIcon: 'partner',
  }),
});

export function approvedBrandId(candidate: unknown): ApprovedBrandId | null {
  return candidate === 'core' || candidate === 'partner' ? candidate : null;
}
